the problem 

One "fat" interface forces every implementing class to implement methods it doesn't need
Symptoms: empty bodies, throw UnsupportedOperationException, NotImplementedError
Example: Worker { work(), eat(), sleep() } → RobotWorker forced to implement eat() and sleep()

there is diff b.w how to solve this problem like we can say in the 2 way we can solve this problem 
using the inteface and using the absctraction

when to use absctract->
Shared state (fields) + shared implementation (concrete methods) -> use abstraction 


when to use inteface -> 
Unrelated classes need the same contract
No shared state / no shared implementation needed


